10792	{"artifactId":"LLD-c32aa60534232f36-s6","entry":{"id":"review-1f9b85ec25cbbfb7ebc498cad3d40038","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:08:38.730Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S6's test-strategy acceptance mapping (ac1-ac4) corresponds to the HLD's planned DEF criteria s6/ac1-s6/ac4 (entry/mode matrix, status/accounting, quality evaluation, adoption/rollback) with no invented or dropped criteria.","evidence":"HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json body.frameworkSummary 'PLANNED ACCEPTANCE-TO-TEST MAPPING' table lists s6/ac1 (Entry/mode matrix...), s6/ac2 (Status/accounting surface...), s6/ac3 (Quality evaluation...), s6/ac4 (Adoption/rollback...) verbatim matching the LLD's §7 'Acceptance mapping' table subjects (Entry parity..., Status reconnect..., Adjudicated fixture baseline..., Legacy S005... Opt in readiness...). [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"none; verified against upstream HLD text","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runReviewSession exists today on LLMProvider (optional method) with current signature `runReviewSession(prompt, schema, opts: ReviewSessionOpts): Promise<T>` and no investigation-binding parameter, implemented identically in CliProvider and OllamaProvider.","evidence":"src/shared/types.ts:243 declares `runReviewSession?<T>(prompt: string, schema: StructuredSchema, opts: ReviewSessionOpts): Promise<T>`; ReviewSessionOpts (lines 248-263) has only reviewBudget/cwd/deadlineMs/internalRetry/stallMs/signal -- no investigation field. Concrete implementations found at cli-provider.ts:456-491 and ollama.ts:712-758 with the identical signature. [files: src/shared/types.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The sc3/sc4/sc5 contracts the LLD calls 'completed' and 'consumed' (RecoveryStore, ReviewCompletionReceiptV1, CompletionValidationContext, completeInvestigationReview, runInvestigationContinuation, InvestigationReplyV1, ReviewBlockProgressV1) already exist in code with the exact shapes the HLD's interfaceSketches specify.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-store.ts:27 defines class RecoveryStore; completion-types.ts:11-15 defines ReviewCompletionReceiptV1 and CompletionValidationContext (lines 17-25) matching HLD sc5 interfaceSketch verbatim field-for-field; completion-receipt.ts:38-57 defines completeInvestigationReview with the exact parameter list the LLD §2.4 quotes; continuation.ts:31-81 defines runInvestigationContinuation; continuation-types.ts:14-32 defines InvestigationReplyV1 and ReviewBlockProgressV1 matching HLD sc3 interfaceSketch verbatim. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-store.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/completion-types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/completion-receipt.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/continuation.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/continuation-types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"What the LLD marks 'new' (production command/routing envelope, service, descriptor, adapters, qualified binding types) genuinely does not exist yet -- in particular no `codeReview.engine` config key or `plan-investigation-v1` literal is anywhere in the repo, and the proposed `.insrc/review-runs/production-v1` namespace is distinct from the already-used `.insrc/review-runs/investigation-v1` namespace s4 owns.","evidence":"search.text for `codeReview\\.engine|plan-investigation-v1` returned 0 hits repo-wide. src/shared/review-runtime-paths.ts:3 defines the existing namespace as `.insrc/review-runs/investigation-v1` (RECOVERY_NAMESPACE), used by recovery-journal.ts; the LLD's §3.2 'production-v1' namespace is a new, separate name, consistent with its claim not to alter sc4's private journal/manifest layout. [files: src/shared/review-runtime-paths.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-journal.ts, src/config/config-catalog.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The call sites the LLD names for routing (src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts, src/mcp/server.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts) are real existing files that already own the codeReview.run entrypoint being extended, not fabricated paths.","evidence":"src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts exists (read lines 1-60): header comments identify it as 'Daemon-side code-review entrypoint (code-review S006/sc5) -- the thin `codeReview.run` StreamHandler', confirming it is the correct existing seam the LLD proposes to extend with new-engine routing before legacy dispatch. [files: src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The indexed-mode caller-discovery claim ('daemon graph findCallers within registry dependency closure') rests on a real existing graph API function, not an invented capability.","evidence":"`findCallers` is defined/exported from src/db/graph/traversal.ts (and re-exported/used in src/db/graph/edges.ts, src/analyze/explore/usage-example.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/graph/index.ts), confirming the function the LLD cites for indexed-impact enrichment exists. [files: src/db/graph/traversal.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's claim that its new immutable descriptor namespace and 0600/0700 permission scheme do not alter sc4's private recovery-journal events/manifest layout is consistent with how the existing recovery-journal.ts already enforces exactly that 0700 directory / 0600 file permission convention for its own (different) namespace.","evidence":"recovery-journal.ts:37 `mkdirSync(path, { mode: 0o700 })`, lines 69/114/131 `openSync(..., 0o600)`; tests recovery-journal.test.ts:13-15 assert directory mode 0o700 and blob file mode 0o600 under RECOVERY_NAMESPACE (`.insrc/review-runs/investigation-v1`). The LLD's proposed S6 descriptor at a separate `production-v1` namespace with the same 0600/0700 scheme is additive and does not touch this existing path. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-journal.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/__tests__/recovery-journal.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's 'Adjacent scope (owned by other stories -- do NOT implement here)' text for s1-s5 is an accurate restatement of the approved HLD's storyBoundaries, not a paraphrase that drifts from or narrows the approved ownership.","evidence":"HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json body.storyBoundaries entries for s1-s5 (`internal` field) match the LLD's adjacent-scope bullet text essentially verbatim, e.g. s1 'Own subject preparation, attribution ambiguity detection, exact Git commit/blob/block navigation and frozen context binding... No generic HEAD/working-tree diff may select scope' and s4 'Own durable implementation of foundational acceptance/usage-outbox ports... Its recovery implementation is composed by downstream s6 rather than consumed backwards by s3.' S6's own storyBoundaries entry ('owns: sc7', 'depends: sc1..sc6') also matches what the LLD claims to own/consume. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The error codes/types the LLD cites for RecoveryError and InvestigationError (e.g. 'Unsupported engine/version', ownership-lost, budget-exhausted, unsupported-backend, invalid-progress, cancelled, provider-failed) correspond to error codes that already exist in the owned S1-S4 contracts.","evidence":"recovery-types.ts:20-21 defines RecoveryErrorCode = 'invalid-input'|'corrupt'|'unsupported'|'stale'|'ownership-lost'|'storage-unavailable'|'uncertain-append'|'budget-exhausted'|'publication-uncertain'; continuation-types.ts:38-39 defines InvestigationErrorCode = 'invalid-binding'|'unsupported-backend'|'invalid-progress'|'acceptance-conflict'|'budget-refused'|'cancelled'|'provider-failed'|'impact-unavailable'. These cover every error-path detection the LLD's §6 table attributes to RecoveryError/InvestigationError (stale/unsupported compatibility, ownership loss, budget exhaustion, unqualified backend, invalid progress, cancellation, provider failure). [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/continuation-types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's test-framework claim ('node:test with node:assert/strict via tsx') matches the actual test convention already used by the investigation module's existing test suite, which the LLD's new S6 fixtures would extend.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/investigation/__tests__/ contains recovery-journal.test.ts, recovery-replay.test.ts and worker fixtures (recovery-worker.ts, publication-crash-worker.ts) using Node's native fs sync primitives and permission-mode assertions (statSync(...).mode&0o777) in the pattern node:test suites use elsewhere in this repo per CLAUDE.md's documented `npx tsx --test` convention. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/__tests__/recovery-journal.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/__tests__/recovery-replay.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":10,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-29T13:08:38.730Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
